{
  "area": "usvi-st-thomas-st-john",
  "method": "St Thomas and St John, US Virgin Islands, including the Buck Island and Capella Island cluster off Bolongo Bay, the St James and Pillsbury Sound cays, Thatch Cay, Congo and Carval, and St John's national-park and south-shore sites; Water Island is covered by the same operators. St Croix and the BVI are separate areas. Lists used: five independent operator lists (Aqua Action Dive Center, whose owner now also holds the Coki Dive Center brand, so the two count once; Red Hook Dive Center, whose three area pages are image maps read as pictures; JJ Divers; Aqua Marine Dive Center; St Thomas Dive Center), the USVI Department of Tourism pages for St Thomas and St John (one list, counted once), and the NPS Submerged Resources dive guide to Virgin Islands National Park (read from an archived 2023 snapshot because the live page now returns 404; the 2012 text predates the current interactive mooring map, so it counts as the single official list). The NPS live mooring map, the USVI DPNR mooring list, and Coral Reef National Monument have no readable named dive-site list. Low Key Watersports, Cruz Bay Watersports, Coki Dive Center (closed, sold to Aqua Action) and Blue Island Divers (domain lapsed) publish no named site list, and Patagon Dive Center is closed; none of them is counted. A site is counted when named on at least two independent lists and recreationally divable on scuba; one-list names, snorkel-only sites, and duplicates are kept as excluded rows. Cow Rock and Calf Rock are two dives by Aqua Action and Red Hook but one dive elsewhere, so they are one row. No list gives coordinates, so no positions are recorded. Counted 2026-10-14.",
